      "craftBreakdown": {
        "setupSummary": "Establishes the sensory reality of Port Orford at dawn, Maeve's daily routine watching dead juvenile rockfish spill onto the decks, and the gap between her flawless lab design and the fishermen's economic reality.",
        "turnOrMisdirection": "The audience expects Maeve to win Roy over with better data or a dramatic tank test. Instead, the turn comes when she admits he was right about the kelp, leaves her clipboard behind, and asks him to teach her how to mend a net.",
        "payoffOrTag": "Transition directly into how your own company or team stopped lecturing customers and started sitting beside them in the rain.",
        "whyItLands": "It strips away founder arrogance. Rather than positioning the protagonist as a visionary who conquered doubters, it frames the mission's true origin as the moment she earned the right to be heard by respecting the craft of the people she wanted to help."
      },
